WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.251 --> 00:00:03.251
(rock music)
(cheering)

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:05.576
- The first time I laid
down the guitar track

00:00:05.576 --> 00:00:07.986
and then played the fiddle on top of this,

00:00:07.986 --> 00:00:10.037
it make me have goose bump on my arm,

00:00:10.037 --> 00:00:12.389
'cause like this is something shamanic.

00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:14.806
(rock music)

00:00:24.579 --> 00:00:27.200
My name's Nature
Ganganbaigal; I am a musician.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.617
I'm originally from China, but
I have a Mongolian ancestry.

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:33.291
(mournful fiddle music)

00:00:33.291 --> 00:00:35.176
So this our Mongolian fiddle,

00:00:35.176 --> 00:00:36.648
we call them (speaking foreign language),

00:00:36.648 --> 00:00:40.232
or in the English we can
say horsehead fiddle.

00:00:40.232 --> 00:00:43.949
(fiddle music)
(throat singing)

00:00:43.949 --> 00:00:45.901
Throat singing is a very ancient

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:48.349
and traditional way of singing.

00:00:48.349 --> 00:00:52.329
You press your throat, and
you generate one sound,

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:54.499
but then you generate an overtone

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:56.349
on the top of it, within your mouth,

00:00:56.349 --> 00:00:59.570
so it sounds like two
sounds at the same time.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.737
(fiddle music)
(throat singing)

00:01:04.779 --> 00:01:08.011
With the next song, I'll
ask you first one question:

00:01:08.011 --> 00:01:09.939
who ride a horse before?

00:01:09.939 --> 00:01:11.379
(cheering)

00:01:11.379 --> 00:01:13.028
If you read the Mongolian history,

00:01:13.028 --> 00:01:15.928
it's all about those brave warrior conquer

00:01:15.928 --> 00:01:18.267
all around the world and
then they don't fear death.

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:20.131
You know, that kind of spirit.

00:01:20.131 --> 00:01:24.537
(wordless vocalizing)
(rock music)

00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:26.707
Metal people, heavy metal
people, it's also like,

00:01:26.707 --> 00:01:28.611
very, mentally, you don't give a shit,

00:01:28.611 --> 00:01:30.151
you just do whatever you want.

00:01:30.151 --> 00:01:33.733
Like this free spirit,
definitely free spirit in it.

00:01:33.733 --> 00:01:36.150
(rock music)

00:01:37.685 --> 00:01:40.280
People will say, "Oh, why you
are doing Mongolian music?"

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:42.744
They don't understand
the whole ancestry thing.

00:01:42.744 --> 00:01:45.195
They don't understand your
own cultural identity.

00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:47.773
But at the end of the day, I
love the Mongolian culture.

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:49.840
And that's all what it matters.

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.257
(rock music)

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:59.283
(cheering)
Thank you!

